        <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900">Buyer Terms</h1>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> October 1, 2026 <strong>Version:</strong> 2.1</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">These Buyer Terms ("Terms") govern your participation as a Buyer on the BreederHQ Marketplace, including browsing listings, joining waitlists, paying reservation fees, purchasing animals, booking breeding services, and booking services from Service Providers. These Terms supplement and are incorporated into the BreederHQ Terms of Service, the Acceptable Use Policy, the Marketplace Transaction Terms, and the Legal Definitions Schedule.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">"Buyer," "you," and "your" refer to any individual who browses, inquires about, reserves, or purchases animals or services through the BreederHQ Marketplace.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms used in these Terms have the meanings given in the BreederHQ Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">2. Account Requirements</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.1 Registration</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">To participate in transactions on the Marketplace, you must create a BreederHQ account with accurate and current information. You must be at least 18 years of age (or the age of majority in your jurisdiction).</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">2.2 Accurate Information</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You agree to provide truthful information in your account profile, inquiries, and communications with Providers. Misrepresentation of your identity, intentions, or capacity to complete a transaction may result in account suspension or termination.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">3. Browsing, Inquiries, and Reliance</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.1 Listing Information; Credential Displays; Profile Indicators</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Listings on the Marketplace, including all descriptions, photos, health claims, pedigree data, service descriptions, pricing, and any credential displays, Profile Indicators, badges, or other indicators displayed in connection with a Provider's profile or listing, are created or attested by Providers, not by BreederHQ. <strong>BreederHQ does not verify, endorse, evaluate, validate, or guarantee the accuracy, authenticity, currency, or completeness of any such content, except as expressly limited by §2.5 of the Terms of Service (Third-Party Registry Passthrough) and §2.6 of the Terms of Service (Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough).</strong> BreederHQ does not open, read, or evaluate any document a Provider uploads in connection with a credential attestation; the act of BreederHQ displaying or linking to such a document is not a representation by BreederHQ as to the document's authenticity, currency, or contents.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.2 Due Diligence; Buyer Acknowledgment</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>You acknowledge and agree that BreederHQ has not conducted, and is under no obligation to conduct, any of the following due-diligence steps on your behalf with respect to any Provider, animal, or listing. You are solely responsible for conducting your own due diligence before entering into any transaction.</strong> Without limiting the foregoing, we strongly recommend that you:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Research the Provider's reputation, experience, and history;</li><li>Request and review health testing documentation and veterinary records;</li><li>Verify registration, pedigree, and credential claims through the relevant breed registry, issuing body, or licensing authority;</li><li>Ask the Provider detailed questions about the animal's history, temperament, and care, or about the scope and methods of any service to be rendered;</li><li>Arrange an in-person visit or live video call to see the animal or facility before purchase when possible;</li><li>Request and review the Provider's written contract, health guarantee, service agreement, and refund or cancellation policy before committing;</li><li>Consult your own veterinarian for guidance on health evaluations.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where a Provider has uploaded a Supporting Document or has indicated holding a professional credential, license, or accreditation, <strong>you are responsible for independently confirming the credential with the issuing body</strong> before relying on it. The presence of a document link on the Services is not a substitute for that confirmation.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.3 Communication</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All communications between you and Providers conducted through the BreederHQ messaging system are subject to the BreederHQ Terms of Service. You agree to communicate respectfully and in good faith.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">3.4 Provider Insurance and Licensing — Your Responsibility, Not BreederHQ's</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Where applicable to a Provider's profession or services (for example, a farrier, trainer, veterinarian, groomer, transporter, or pet sitter), the Provider may be required by applicable law to maintain professional licensing, insurance, or both. <strong>BreederHQ does not require, evaluate, verify, hold, broker, or facilitate any such licensing or insurance, and BreederHQ makes no representation that any Provider holds any such licensing or insurance.</strong> You are encouraged to confirm directly with the Provider, and with the applicable issuing body or insurance carrier, whether the Provider holds the licensing and insurance you consider necessary for your transaction. <strong>BreederHQ disclaims all liability for any harm arising from a Provider's lack of, lapse in, or misrepresentation of licensing or insurance.</strong></p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">4. Waitlist Participation</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.1 Joining a Waitlist</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When you join a Provider's waitlist and pay a reservation fee, you are entering into a direct agreement with the Provider, not with BreederHQ. Before paying a reservation fee, you should:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Understand the Provider's reservation fee amount and what it covers;</li><li>Read and agree to the Provider's refund policy;</li><li>Understand the Provider's selection process and timeline;</li><li>Confirm whether the reservation fee is refundable, partially refundable, or non-refundable.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.2 Reservation Fee Payments</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A reservation fee is a payment obligation arising between you and the Provider, and is owed and payable to the Provider. Payment is collected at checkout by our third-party payment processor for the Provider. <strong>BreederHQ does not act as an escrow agent and does not hold reservation fees in trust for you or for the Provider. BreederHQ does not guarantee, insure, or backstop any reservation fee, and has no obligation to refund a reservation fee out of its own funds.</strong> Whether a refund is owed is governed by the Provider's stated refund policy and applicable law. <strong>The Provider is responsible for funding and authorizing any refund owed to you</strong>; where a refund is authorized, it is executed through the payment processor or, where a payment was routed through BreederHQ's payment infrastructure, through that infrastructure. <strong>Nothing in these Terms limits any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be waived, including any rights you may have under card network rules or against your card issuer.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.3 Waitlist Position</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Your position on a waitlist is managed by the Provider. BreederHQ does not control or guarantee:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Your position on any waitlist;</li><li>The timeline for availability of animals;</li><li>The Provider's selection process or criteria;</li><li>That a suitable animal will be available for you.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">4.4 No Guarantee of Placement</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Joining a waitlist does not guarantee that you will receive an animal. Litter outcomes, Provider selection processes, and other factors may affect availability. If the Provider is unable to fulfill your reservation, the Provider's refund policy applies.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">5. Purchases</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.1 Direct Transaction</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">All purchases are direct transactions between you and the Provider. By completing a purchase, you agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Pay the agreed-upon price through the payment method provided;</li><li>Arrange and pay for transportation/delivery as agreed with the Provider;</li><li>Comply with all applicable laws regarding animal acquisition and transport in your jurisdiction;</li><li>Provide appropriate care for the animal upon receipt.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2 Payment Processing</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Payments are processed by our third-party payment processor. By making a payment, you agree to the payment processor's terms of service. <strong>BreederHQ does not receive, hold, or have access to your payment card number or other card credentials.</strong> Depending on the transaction, BreederHQ may provide payment-related platform or settlement services as described in §2.7 of the Terms of Service.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.2A Taxes</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Prices shown are set by the Provider. Where tax applies to a transaction, it may be added to your total and will be shown at or before checkout when it is applied. <strong>If a price, total, or receipt does not show a tax line, or shows tax as zero, that does not mean no tax applies to your purchase.</strong></p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">5.3 Purchase Agreement</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">We strongly recommend that you obtain a written purchase agreement from the Provider that includes:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Complete description of the animal being purchased;</li><li>Total purchase price and payment terms;</li><li>Health guarantee terms and duration;</li><li>Spay/neuter requirements (if any);</li><li>Return and refund policy;</li><li>Registration transfer details;</li><li>Any other conditions or requirements.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ is not responsible for enforcing any agreement between you and a Provider.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">6. Breeding Service Bookings and Service Provider Bookings</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.1 Service Agreement</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">When booking a breeding service (stud service, semen purchase, etc.) or a service from a Service Provider (farrier, trainer, veterinarian, groomer, transporter, etc.), the terms of the service are between you and the Provider. Before booking, confirm:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Service type, scope, methods, pricing, and payment schedule;</li><li>For breeding services: breeding method (live cover, AI, shipped semen, etc.), return breeding or guarantee terms, required health testing and documentation;</li><li>For Service Provider bookings: the qualifications and experience of the individual(s) who will render the service, the service location, any limitations on service, and the Service Provider's cancellation and refund policy;</li><li>Timeline and scheduling details.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">6.2 Outcome Acknowledgment</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You acknowledge that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Breeding outcomes (including conception, litter size, and offspring health) are inherently unpredictable; neither the Provider nor BreederHQ guarantees any specific breeding outcome;</li><li>Services rendered by Service Providers are subject to the inherent unpredictability of working with animals; outcomes (including animal response to training, treatment, transport, or grooming) cannot be guaranteed.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">7. Refunds and Disputes</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.1 Provider Refund and Cancellation Policies</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Refund and cancellation terms for purchases, reservation fees, and services are established by each Provider. BreederHQ does not set, manage, or enforce Provider refund or cancellation policies.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.2 Resolving Disputes</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">If a dispute arises with a Provider, you should:</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">1. Contact the Provider directly to attempt resolution in good faith; 2. Document all communications and agreements; 3. If you believe fraud has occurred, report it to BreederHQ at <strong>legal@breederhq.com</strong>; 4. You may also contact your payment provider (bank or credit card company) to explore chargeback options if applicable.</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">7.3 BreederHQ's Role</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ is not a party to your transaction and has no obligation to resolve disputes between you and a Provider. However, BreederHQ may:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Review fraud reports and take action against Provider accounts that violate platform policies;</li><li>Suspend display of a disputed credential pending the Provider's response under the procedure in §8.4 of the Acceptable Use Policy;</li><li>Provide transaction records upon request, subject to privacy considerations;</li><li>Suspend or remove Providers who demonstrate a pattern of bad faith conduct.</li></ul>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Any suspension-of-display or other action BreederHQ takes is an exercise of platform discretion in response to a credible report; it is not BreederHQ's adjudication of the underlying truth of any claim.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">8. Buyer Responsibilities</h2>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.1 Legal Compliance</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You are responsible for complying with all applicable laws in your jurisdiction regarding:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Animal ownership and possession;</li><li>Import/transport regulations (interstate or international);</li><li>Local zoning or housing restrictions for animals;</li><li>Species or breed-specific legislation;</li><li>Required permits, licenses, or registrations.</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.2 Animal Welfare</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">By acquiring an animal through the Marketplace or by retaining a Service Provider to render services to an animal in your possession, you agree to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Provide appropriate food, water, shelter, veterinary care, and socialization;</li><li>Not use the animal for any illegal purpose, including animal fighting;</li><li>Comply with any contractual obligations agreed upon with the Provider (such as spay/neuter requirements or co-ownership terms).</li></ul>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-2 text-gray-900">8.3 Assumption of Risk</h3>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You acknowledge and accept that:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Animals are living beings with inherent and unpredictable health and behavioral risks;</li><li>No amount of health testing, veterinary screening, or genetic analysis can guarantee the future health or temperament of an animal;</li><li>You assume all risks associated with animal ownership from the time you take possession;</li><li>You assume all risks associated with retaining a Service Provider to render services to an animal in your possession, including risks associated with the Service Provider's professional conduct, on-site safety, and the inherent risks of working with animals;</li><li>BreederHQ has no liability for any injury, illness, death, property damage, or other loss related to an animal acquired through the Marketplace or to services rendered by a Provider engaged through the Marketplace.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">9. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You may NOT:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Submit fraudulent inquiries, reservation fees, or purchases;</li><li>Misrepresent your identity, location, or intentions to a Provider;</li><li>Harass, threaten, or intimidate Providers;</li><li>Submit false or defamatory reviews;</li><li>Attempt to circumvent Marketplace payment processing to avoid platform fees;</li><li>Acquire animals for the purpose of resale without the Provider's knowledge and consent;</li><li>Use the Marketplace for any illegal purpose.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">10. Indemnification</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless BreederHQ LLC, its officers, directors, employees, agents, and affiliates from and against any claims, damages, losses, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising from or related to:</p>
        <ul class="mb-4 ml-6 list-disc space-y-2 text-gray-700"><li>Your breach of these Buyer Terms or any other agreement you have with BreederHQ;</li><li>Your violation of any applicable law in connection with your use of the Services;</li><li>Your acts or omissions in connection with a transaction, including but not limited to the care, transport, or possession of any animal you acquired through the Marketplace;</li><li>Any fraudulent inquiry, payment, or representation you make to a Provider;</li><li>Any claim by a third party arising from your acts or omissions.</li></ul>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">11. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, BREEDERHQ SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR DAMAGES ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE MARKETPLACE OR ANY TRANSACTION WITH A PROVIDER TO THE EXTENT CAUSED BY THE ACTS, OMISSIONS, OR REPRESENTATIONS OF A PROVIDER OR ANY OTHER THIRD PARTY, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO DAMAGES RELATED TO ANIMAL HEALTH, ANIMAL BEHAVIOR, DELIVERY, SERVICES RENDERED BY ANY PROVIDER, OR THE FAILURE OF A PROVIDER TO FULFILL COMMITMENTS.</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Nothing in this Section creates liability for BreederHQ. Any liability BreederHQ has to you is governed exclusively by §4.3 of the Terms of Service, including its exclusions, aggregate cap, carve-outs in §4.3(c), and the consumer-rights savings in §4.3(d) and §10.5 (State-Specific Provisions). Nothing in these Buyer Terms limits any right or remedy that cannot lawfully be limited or waived.</strong></p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">12. Modifications</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">BreederHQ may update these Buyer Terms from time to time. Material changes will be communicated to users via email or platform notification at least thirty (30) days before taking effect. Continued use of the Marketplace after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated Buyer Terms.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">13. Definitions</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Capitalized terms not defined in these Terms have the meanings set forth in the Legal Definitions Schedule, which is incorporated into these Terms by reference. The terms "Provider Content," "Supporting Documentation," "Third-Party Registry Passthrough," "Third-Party Identity Verification Passthrough," "Profile Indicator," "Credential Attestation," "Credential Dispute," "Breeder/Seller Provider," and "Service Provider" are defined in the Legal Definitions Schedule.</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3 text-gray-900">14. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">For questions regarding these Buyer Terms, contact:</p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>BreederHQ LLC</strong> Email: legal@breederhq.com</p>
        <hr class="my-8 border-gray-200" />
        <p class="mb-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">_By participating in any transaction on the BreederHQ Marketplace as a Buyer, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Buyer Terms._</p>

        <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 text-sm text-gray-600">
          <p>
            Questions about this document can go to
            <a href="mailto:legal@breederhq.com" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">legal@breederhq.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3">
            <a href="/legal" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,45%)] underline">All legal documents</a>
